      "observed": "T2 is an AON6407 P-channel MOSFET, but its pin 2 (source) is connected to the fused input net /+24V_{F} and its pin 3 (drain) is connected to the protected +24V rail.",
      "expected": "For the reverse-polarity protection implied by the specification/README, a P-channel MOSFET in the 24 V input path should have its source on the protected +24V rail and its drain on the fused input side (/+24V_{F}); this orientation lets the intrinsic body diode and gate zener turn the device on for correct polarity and block reverse polarity.",
