        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"T2\") (value \"AON6407\") ... description \"P-Channel 30 V 32A 10mΩ AON6407\""},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"6\") (name \"/+24V_{F}\") ... (node (ref \"T2\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"S\") ...)"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"3\") (name \"+24V\") ... (node (ref \"T2\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"D\") ...)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "README states the PCB includes \"reverse polarity protection, TVS diodes, proper isolation\""}
      ],
      "impact": "With the source on the input side, the MOSFET body diode conducts when the 24 V supply is reversed, defeating reverse-polarity protection and potentially causing high current, fuse blow, or board damage.",
      "confidence": 0.65
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most of the netlist matches the intended OPNhydro-r2 architecture, but the input P-channel MOSFET T2 appears to be source/drain reversed for reverse-polarity protection."
}

